  "type": "MCQ",
  "question": "Let $f,g$ be differentiable functions on the real line $\\mathbb R$ with $f(0)>g(0)$. Assume that the set $M=\\{t\\in\\mathbb R\\mid f(t)=g(t)\\}$ is non-empty and that $f\\prime(t)\\ge g\\prime(t)$ for all $t\\in M$. Then which of the following is necessarily true?",
  "options": {
    "A": "If $t\\in M$, then $t<0$.",
    "B": "For any $t\\in M$, $f\\prime(t)>g\\prime(t)$.",
    "C": "For any $t\\notin M$, $f(t)>g(t)$.",
    "D": "None of the above."
  },
